### Why this is a product, not research

The city is the FastOps AI product architecture. Microsoft Presidio anonymizes customer data before it enters the multi-model network — PII is stripped so models never see raw customer data, only the problem. This solves the enterprise objection ("how can we trust 300 models with our data?") and unlocks a capability no competitor can replicate: multi-architecture intelligence at scale with data safety built in. The research findings (blind spot detection, mutual correction, routing by demonstrated strength) become product features that literally cannot be built with a single-model architecture. Every piece of city infrastructure you build is a piece of the product.

### What success looks like

1. A problem enters the city (customer data anonymized via Presidio)
2. It gets decomposed and routed to models based on demonstrated strengths (not assumed capabilities)
3. Models work pieces independently, with memory of prior work
4. Results get cross-checked by different architectures (blind spot detection)
5. Disagreements trigger autonomous dialogue (no curator needed)
6. Findings accumulate in the Forge (persistent, shared knowledge)
7. The output is categorically better than any single model could produce
8. Results are de-anonymized and returned — the customer gets multi-architecture intelligence without security risk

